{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat AGENTS.md && cat research/harness/src/{main,data}.js research/harness/src/libs/{uplot,chartjs}.js research/harness/{vite.config.js,package.json,.gitignore}'","aggregated_output":"# Working in this repository\n\nAxylo is a browser charting library. The product is specified in `docs/02-product-spec.md`; the build plan is `docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md`. Read the sections your task names before writing code.\n\n## Rules for every change\n\n- **Contracts are fixed.** `packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts` and `packages/axylo/src/public.ts` are the interfaces between modules. Do not edit them. If your work needs a change there, stop that part, finish what you can, and describe the exact change you need in your report.\n- **Stay in your files.** Each task lists the directories it owns. Do not create, edit or delete anything else, including configuration and other modules. Several agents work in this checkout at the same time.\n- **No runtime dependencies.** Use the platform (`Intl`, typed arrays). Dev dependencies already installed: TypeScript, Vitest, fast-check, esbuild, Playwright (system Chrome), axe-core. The network is not available; do not try to install anything.\n- **No DOM at import time.** A module that needs the DOM takes it as a parameter or touches it inside a function. Pure stages (data, scales, formatting, layout, scene) must run in Node.\n- **Hot paths use typed arrays.** No object per data point, no array of arrays per data point, no copying of large columns that the contracts say are borrowed.\n- **Never guess silently.** Anything that cannot be drawn as given is reported through the `DiagnosticSink` with the code from spec section 3.5.\n- **Tests come from the spec.** Expected values are derived from the specification and the fixture data, never by running the implementation and pasting its output. Use fast-check property tests for invariants (\"for any data …\"). A test you cannot make pass is reported as failing; do not weaken it or change its expected value.\n- **TypeScript strict, no `any`** in exported signatures. `__DEV__` is a build-time boolean (true in tests).\n- **Comments say why**, not what. Names are plain words.\n- **Do not commit.** The coordinator commits.\n\n## Commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run typecheck      # tsc over the library, its tests, and the API examples in docs/api\nnpm test               # unit and property tests (Node)\nnpm run build          # packages/axylo/dist\nnpm run test:browser   # browser tests against the built bundle, in system Chrome\n```\n\n## Your report\n\nEnd with a short report: what you built (files), what you verified and how (paste the last lines of the test run), what is not done or not verified, any contract change you need, and any place where the spec was ambiguous and what you assumed. Keep \"ran and saw\" apart from \"expect\".\nimport * as data from './data.js';\nconst mods = import.meta.glob('./libs/*.{js,jsx}');\nconst q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nconst lib = q.get('lib'), task = q.get('task') ?? 'trend', n = Number(q.get('n') ?? 100000);\nconst el = document.getElementById('chart');\nif (q.get('w')) el.style.width = q.get('w') + 'px';\nif (q.get('scheme')) document.documentElement.style.colorScheme = q.get('scheme'); // e.g. a light-only page under a dark OS\nconst mark = name => window.__mark ? window.__mark(name) : null; // the probe records CDP main-thread metrics at these points\nconst raf = () => new Promise(r => requestAnimationFrame(() => r()));\nwindow.__result = null;\n(async () => {\n  const key = Object.keys(mods).find(k => k.startsWith(`./libs/${lib}.`));\n  if (!key) { el.textContent = 'usage: ?lib=<name>&task=<trend|bars|parts|dirty|scale|stream>'; return; }\n  try {\n    const m = await mods[key]();\n    const one = task.startsWith('dirty-') ? task.slice(6) : null;\n    const fn = task === 'empty' ? m.trend : one ? m.dirty : m[task];\n    if (!fn) { window.__result = { unsupported: true }; el.textContent = `${lib}: ${task} not supported`; return; }\n    // \"empty\": the trend chart when the query returned no rows\n    const d = task === 'scale' ? data.scale(n) : task === 'stream' ? data.stream()\n      : task === 'empty' ? { ...data.trend, title: 'Daily sessions by channel', t: [], series: data.trend.series.map(s => ({ ...s, values: [] })) }\n      : one ? data.dirtyOne(one)\n      : data[task];\n    await raf();\n    await mark('create:start');\n    const t0 = performance.now();\n    const handle = await fn(el, d);\n    const t1 = performance.now();\n    await raf(); await raf();\n    const t2 = performance.now();\n    window.__handle = handle;\n    const res = { createMs: t1 - t0, toPaintMs: t2 - t0 };\n    if (window.__mark) { await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1600)); await mark('create:end'); } // long enough for entry animations to finish\n    if (task === 'stream') {\n      // let entry animations settle, then push one point per frame\n      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1500));\n      const frames = Number(q.get('frames') ?? 300), push = [], gaps = [];\n      await mark('stream:start');\n      let last = performance.now();\n      for (let i = 0; i < frames; i++) {\n        const [x, y] = d.next();\n        const a = performance.now(); handle.push(x, y); push.push(performance.now() - a);\n        await raf(); const now = performance.now(); gaps.push(now - last); last = now;\n      }\n      await raf(); await mark('stream:end');\n      const pct = (arr, p) => [...arr].sort((a, b) => a - b)[Math.min(arr.length - 1, Math.floor(arr.length * p))];\n      Object.assign(res, { pushP50: pct(push, 0.5), pushP95: pct(push, 0.95), frameP50: pct(gaps, 0.5), frameP95: pct(gaps, 0.95), framesOver20ms: gaps.filter(g => g > 20).length, frames });\n    }\n    window.__result = res;\n  } catch (e) { console.error(e); window.__result = { error: String(e?.stack ?? e) }; }\n})();\n// Shared, deterministic datasets. Every library receives exactly these values.\nexport function rng(seed) {\n  let s = seed >>> 0;\n  return () => { s = (s + 0x6D2B79F5) | 0; let t = Math.imul(s ^ (s >>> 15), 1 | s); t = (t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), 61 | t)) ^ t; return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296; };\n}\nconst DAY = 864e5;\nconst START = Date.UTC(2026, 0, 1);\n\n// Task \"trend\": 3 series x 120 daily points (UTC midnights). \"Referral\" has a 7-day outage (nulls).\nexport const trend = (() => {\n  const r = rng(7), n = 120;\n  const t = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => START + i * DAY);\n  const mk = (base, growth, noise, season) => t.map((_, i) => Math.round(base + growth * i + season * Math.sin((i / 7) * 2 * Math.PI) + (r() - 0.5) * noise));\n  const series = [\n    { name: 'Direct', values: mk(31000, 120, 4000, 3000) },\n    { name: 'Organic search', values: mk(18000, 60, 3000, 2500) },\n    { name: 'Referral', values: mk(4200, -8, 1200, 400) },\n  ];\n  for (let i = 60; i < 67; i++) series[2].values[i] = null;\n  return { title: 'Daily sessions by channel', yTitle: 'Sessions', t, series };\n})();\n\n// Task \"bars\": one series, all values between 82 and 97 (tests zero baseline), one long label.\nexport const bars = {\n  title: 'Customer satisfaction by team', yTitle: 'Satisfied (%)', name: 'Satisfied (%)',\n  categories: ['Billing', 'Customer Success & Onboarding', 'Platform', 'Mobile', 'Data', 'Security', 'Sales Eng.'],\n  values: [94, 88, 97, 82, 91, 85, 90],\n};\n\n// Task \"parts\": six shares, two of them small.\nexport const parts = {\n  title: 'Sessions by browser', name: 'Share (%)',\n  labels: ['Chrome', 'Safari', 'Edge', 'Firefox', 'Samsung Internet', 'Other'],\n  values: [46.2, 27.5, 14.1, 8.9, 2.1, 1.2],\n};\n\n// Task \"dirty\": values a real app sends by mistake. Correct reading: Wed, Thu, Sat are missing; Fri is ambiguous (a string).\nexport const dirty = {\n  title: 'Dirty input', name: 'Value',\n  categories: ['Mon', 'Tue', 'Wed', 'Thu', 'Fri', 'Sat', 'Sun'],\n  values: [10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70],\n};\n\n// Task \"scale\": one series, n points, one per minute, random walk.\nexport function scale(n) {\n  const r = rng(1), t = new Array(n), y = new Array(n);\n  let v = 100;\n  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { v += (r() - 0.5) * 2; t[i] = START + i * 60000; y[i] = Math.round(v * 100) / 100; }\n  return { title: `${n.toLocaleString('en-US')} points`, name: 'Value', t, y };\n}\n\n// Task \"stream\": 600-point window; the harness then pushes one new point per frame.\nexport function stream() {\n  const d = scale(600);\n  const r = rng(2);\n  let v = d.y[d.y.length - 1], i = d.t.length;\n  return { ...d, title: 'Streaming window', next: () => { v += (r() - 0.5) * 2; return [START + i++ * 60000, Math.round(v * 100) / 100]; } };\n}\n\n// Task \"dates\": the trend series keyed by calendar-date strings (no time, no zone), to separate\n// \"this library shifts instants into the viewer's zone\" from \"this library cannot show a date as a date\".\nexport const dates = { ...trend, days: trend.t.map(t => new Date(t).toISOString().slice(0, 10)) };\n\n// Tasks \"dirty-null\", \"dirty-nan\", \"dirty-string\", \"dirty-undefined\": one bad value at a time, in a line of\n// seven otherwise valid points, so each outcome can be attributed to one kind of input.\nexport function dirtyOne(kind) {\n  const bad = { null: null, nan: NaN, string: '40', undefined: undefined }[kind];\n  return { ...dirty, title: `One bad value: ${kind}`, values: [10, 20, 30, bad, 50, 60, 70] };\n}\nimport uPlot from 'uplot';\nimport 'uplot/dist/uPlot.min.css';\n\nexport const meta = { name: 'uPlot', pkg: 'uplot' };\n// uPlot needs explicit pixel sizes (no auto-resize), explicit stroke colors (no palette), and x in seconds.\nconst size = el => ({ width: el.clientWidth, height: el.clientHeight - 80 }); // title and legend sit outside `height`\nconst colors = ['red', 'green', 'blue']; // the colors used in uPlot's README example\nconst secs = t => t.map(v => v / 1000);\n\nexport function trend(el, d) {\n  const u = new uPlot({\n    title: d.title, ...size(el),\n    series: [{}, ...d.series.map((s, i) => ({ label: s.name, stroke: colors[i] }))],\n    axes: [{}, { label: d.yTitle }],\n  }, [secs(d.t), ...d.series.map(s => s.values)], el);\n  return { u, destroy: () => u.destroy() };\n}\n\nexport function bars(el, d) {\n  const idx = d.categories.map((_, i) => i);\n  const u = new uPlot({\n    title: d.title, ...size(el),\n    scales: { x: { time: false, range: [-0.5, idx.length - 0.5] } },\n    axes: [{ splits: () => idx, values: (u, splits) => splits.map(i => d.categories[i]) }, { label: d.yTitle }],\n    series: [{}, { label: d.name, stroke: 'blue', fill: 'rgba(0,0,255,0.3)', paths: uPlot.paths.bars({ size: [0.6, 100] }) }],\n  }, [idx, d.values], el);\n  return { u, destroy: () => u.destroy() };\n}\n\nexport const parts = null; // no pie/donut in uPlot\n\nexport function dirty(el, d) {\n  const idx = d.categories.map((_, i) => i);\n  const u = new uPlot({\n    title: d.title, ...size(el),\n    scales: { x: { time: false } },\n    axes: [{ splits: () => idx, values: (u, splits) => splits.map(i => d.categories[i]) }, {}],\n    series: [{}, { label: d.name, stroke: 'blue' }],\n  }, [idx, d.values], el);\n  return { u, destroy: () => u.destroy() };\n}\n\nexport function scale(el, d) {\n  const data = [secs(d.t), d.y.slice()];\n  const u = new uPlot({ title: d.title, ...size(el), series: [{}, { label: d.name, stroke: 'blue' }] }, data, el);\n  return { u, data, destroy: () => u.destroy() };\n}\n\nexport function stream(el, d) {\n  const h = scale(el, d);\n  h.push = (x, y) => { h.data[0].push(x / 1000); h.data[0].shift(); h.data[1].push(y); h.data[1].shift(); h.u.setData(h.data); };\n  return h;\n}\n\n// uPlot takes numbers only, so the date strings go through Date.parse (UTC midnight for date-only strings).\nexport function dates(el, d) {\n  const u = new uPlot({ title: d.title, ...size(el), series: [{}, ...d.series.map((s, i) => ({ label: s.name, stroke: colors[i] }))] },\n    [d.days.map(s => Date.parse(s) / 1000), ...d.series.map(s => s.values)], el);\n  return { u, destroy: () => u.destroy() };\n}\nimport { Chart } from 'chart.js/auto';\nimport 'chartjs-adapter-date-fns'; // a date adapter is required before a time scale works\n\nexport const meta = { name: 'Chart.js', pkg: 'chart.js' };\nconst canvas = el => el.appendChild(document.createElement('canvas'));\n// maintainAspectRatio:false is needed for the chart to fill a fixed-height container\nconst base = d => ({ maintainAspectRatio: false, plugins: { title: { display: true, text: d.title } } });\n\nexport function trend(el, d) {\n  const chart = new Chart(canvas(el), {\n    type: 'line',\n    data: { labels: d.t, datasets: d.series.map(s => ({ label: s.name, data: s.values })) },\n    options: { ...base(d), scales: { x: { type: 'time' }, y: { title: { display: true, text: d.yTitle } } } },\n  });\n  return { chart, destroy: () => chart.destroy() };\n}\n\nexport function bars(el, d) {\n  const chart = new Chart(canvas(el), {\n    type: 'bar',\n    data: { labels: d.categories, datasets: [{ label: d.name, data: d.values }] },\n    options: { ...base(d), scales: { y: { title: { display: true, text: d.yTitle } } } },\n  });\n  return { chart, destroy: () => chart.destroy() };\n}\n\nexport function parts(el, d) {\n  const chart = new Chart(canvas(el), {\n    type: 'doughnut',\n    data: { labels: d.labels, datasets: [{ label: d.name, data: d.values }] },\n    options: base(d),\n  });\n  return { chart, destroy: () => chart.destroy() };\n}\n\nexport function dirty(el, d) {\n  const chart = new Chart(canvas(el), {\n    type: 'line',\n    data: { labels: d.categories, datasets: [{ label: d.name, data: d.values }] },\n    options: base(d),\n  });\n  return { chart, destroy: () => chart.destroy() };\n}\n\nexport function scale(el, d) {\n  const chart = new Chart(canvas(el), {\n    type: 'line',\n    data: { labels: d.t, datasets: [{ label: d.name, data: d.y }] },\n    options: { ...base(d), scales: { x: { type: 'time' } } },\n  });\n  return { chart, destroy: () => chart.destroy() };\n}\n\nexport function stream(el, d) {\n  const h = scale(el, d), { chart } = h;\n  h.push = (x, y) => {\n    chart.data.labels.push(x); chart.data.labels.shift();\n    chart.data.datasets[0].data.push(y); chart.data.datasets[0].data.shift();\n    chart.update();\n  };\n  return h;\n}\n\nexport function dates(el, d) {\n  const chart = new Chart(canvas(el), {\n    type: 'line',\n    data: { labels: d.days, datasets: d.series.map(s => ({ label: s.name, data: s.values })) },\n    options: { ...base(d), scales: { x: { type: 'time' } } },\n  });\n  return { chart, destroy: () => chart.destroy() };\n}\nimport { defineConfig } from 'vite';\nimport react from '@vitejs/plugin-react';\nexport default defineConfig({ plugins: [react()], build: { target: 'es2022', chunkSizeWarningLimit: 20000 } });\n{\n  \"name\": \"axylo-landscape-harness\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"Runs the same chart tasks through ten charting libraries for the Axylo landscape study.\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"preview\": \"vite preview --port 4173 --strictPort\",\n    \"probe\": \"node probe.mjs\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"@emotion/react\": \"^11.14.0\",\n    \"@emotion/styled\": \"^11.14.1\",\n    \"@mui/material\": \"^9.5.0\",\n    \"@mui/system\": \"^9.5.0\",\n    \"@mui/x-charts\": \"^9.18.1\",\n    \"@nivo/bar\": \"^0.99.0\",\n    \"@nivo/core\": \"^0.99.0\",\n    \"@nivo/line\": \"^0.99.0\",\n    \"@nivo/pie\": \"^0.99.0\",\n    \"apexcharts\": \"^8.9.0\",\n    \"chart.js\": \"^4.6.1\",\n    \"chartjs-adapter-date-fns\": \"^3.0.0\",\n    \"d3\": \"^7.9.2\",\n    \"date-fns\": \"^4.4.0\",\n    \"echarts\": \"^6.1.0\",\n    \"highcharts\": \"^13.1.1\",\n    \"plotly.js-dist-min\": \"^4.3.0\",\n    \"react\": \"^19.3.1\",\n    \"react-dom\": \"^19.3.1\",\n    \"react-is\": \"^19.3.1\",\n    \"recharts\": \"^3.11.0\",\n    \"uplot\": \"^1.6.32\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^6.3.0\",\n    \"esbuild\": \"^0.28.2\",\n    \"playwright-core\": \"^1.65.1\",\n    \"pngjs\": \"^7.0.0\",\n    \"vite\": \"^8.3.8\"\n  }\n}\nnode_modules/\ndist/\npreview.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
