{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat research/harness/index.html && tar -xOzf tests/dist/.packed/axylo-0.0.0.tgz package/package.json && rg -n 'dist:|pack|validate' package.json tests/dist -g '*.json' -g '*.ts' -g '\"'!**/.packed/**'\"' | head -65 && git check-ignore tests/dist/.packed/axylo-0.0.0.tgz\"","aggregated_output":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<title>Axylo landscape harness</title>\n<style>\n  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }\n  body { margin: 16px; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; background: Canvas; color: CanvasText; }\n  #chart { width: 720px; height: 400px; position: relative; }\n  button { font: inherit; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<button id=\"before\">before</button>\n<div id=\"chart\"></div>\n<button id=\"after\">after</button>\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n{\n  \"name\": \"axylo\",\n  \"version\": \"0.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"Everyday charts that are faithful to the data, readable everywhere and accessible by default.\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"sideEffects\": [\"*.css\"],\n  \"files\": [\n    \"dist/axylo.js\",\n    \"dist/axylo.dev.js\",\n    \"dist/axylo.iife.js\",\n    \"dist/axylo.iife.min.js\",\n    \"dist/axylo.css\",\n    \"dist/index.d.ts\",\n    \"dist/public.d.ts\"\n  ],\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n      \"development\": \"./dist/axylo.dev.js\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/axylo.js\"\n    },\n    \"./axylo.css\": \"./dist/axylo.css\"\n  }\n}\npackage.json:6:    \"packages/*\"\npackage.json:9:    \"typecheck\": \"tsc -p packages/axylo --noEmit && tsc -p docs/api && tsc -p tests/dist\",\npackage.json:17:    \"test:dist:browser\": \"AXYLO_BROWSER=1 vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts\",\npackage.json:18:    \"check\": \"npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build && npm run test:browser && npm run test:dist && npm run test:dist:browser && npm run size\"\ntests/dist/node.test.ts:2: * Spec DX8, the Node half, from the packed files in child processes started inside the fixtures (so Node,\ntests/dist/node.test.ts:3: * not Vitest's resolver, finds the packages, and no test-runner globals are present):\ntests/dist/node.test.ts:5: * - `validate()` runs there and reports the Phase 1 `dirty` fixture as spec 3.5 and plan 1.6 say.\ntests/dist/node.test.ts:22:  it('ran without DOM globals, from the packed file', () => {\ntests/dist/node.test.ts:28:  it('exports the five chart functions and validate, and adds no globals on import', () => {\ntests/dist/node.test.ts:29:    expect(probe.exports).toEqual(['area', 'bar', 'donut', 'line', 'scatter', 'validate']);\ntests/dist/node.test.ts:33:  it('validate() reports the dirty fixture: AX102, AX103 and AX106 once each, with field and rows (spec 3.5, plan 1.6)', () => {\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:3: * composition (packages/axylo/src/kinds), so a consumer that imports `line` must not carry the code of\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:19: * The package ships one prebundled file per condition; that it can be shaken at all rests on its doing no work\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:27: * even when the module's own text carries no marker. `validate` alone must carry no drawing, DOM, lookup or\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:67:  // statement does nothing. With `ignoreAnnotations` esbuild disregards the package's `sideEffects` promise, so\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:102:/** Source modules that belong to some kinds only (paths under packages/axylo/src), and the kinds they belong to. */\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:115:const src = path.join(repo, 'packages/axylo/src');\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:117:async function sourceModules(name: Kind | 'validate'): Promise<Set<string>> {\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:139:  it('validate: includes no composition and no drawing, DOM, lookup or reader module', async () => {\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:140:    const modules = await sourceModules('validate');\ntests/dist/tree-shaking.test.ts:141:    expect(modules.has('data/normalize.ts'), 'validate normalizes').toBe(true);\ntests/dist/flavours.browser.test.ts:11: * Each row runs on all four packed core files: the ESM development and default files (through the\ntests/dist/paths.ts:7:// @ts-expect-error scripts/pack.mjs is plain JavaScript without declarations\ntests/dist/paths.ts:8:import { fixtureGuard as untypedGuard } from '../../scripts/pack.mjs';\ntests/dist/paths.ts:12:export const packed = path.join(here, '.packed');\ntests/dist/paths.ts:22:  unpackedSize: number;\ntests/dist/paths.ts:23:  /** Paths inside the tarball, without the `package/` prefix, as npm pack listed them. */\ntests/dist/paths.ts:26:export interface Manifest { packedAt: string; packages: Record<'axylo', PackedPackage> }\ntests/dist/paths.ts:28:export const manifest = (): Manifest => JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(packed, 'manifest.json'), 'utf8')) as Manifest;\ntests/dist/paths.ts:44:/** The package.json as it was packed (read from the unpacked tarball, not from the workspace). */\ntests/dist/paths.ts:45:export const packedJson = (name: 'axylo'): PackageJson =>\ntests/dist/paths.ts:46:  JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(installed(name, 'package.json'), 'utf8')) as PackageJson;\ntests/dist/paths.ts:48:/** A file of a package as unpacked into the fixture that installs it. */\ntests/dist/paths.ts:100:/** esbuild plugin (scripts/pack.mjs): any import that resolves outside `roots` fails the build. */\ntests/dist/types.test.ts:2: * The packed declarations type-check an application (strict, skipLibCheck off), under both\ntests/dist/types.test.ts:3: * module resolutions a TypeScript consumer of an ESM package uses: `Bundler` (bundled applications) and\ntests/dist/types.test.ts:15:] as const)('%s fixture', (name, packages, snippet) => {\ntests/dist/types.test.ts:20:    it('type-checks with tsc --strict against the packed declarations', () => {\ntests/dist/types.test.ts:25:    it('read every declaration from inside the fixture, the packed ones from its node_modules', () => {\ntests/dist/types.test.ts:27:      for (const pkg of packages) {\ntests/dist/text.browser.test.ts:15: * csp.browser.test.ts, from the packed script-tag file and from a bundled module.\ntests/dist/browser.ts:3: * for the distribution's browser tests. packages/axylo/test/browser/harness.ts is not reused: it serves the\ntests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:3: * fixture) renders from the packed files in system Chrome, by npm and by script tag: a figure with an\ntests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:7: * a generated name, and raises only AX140), and importing the package changes nothing in the document (the\ntests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:12: * package-level parts (resolution, loading, styles) carry over, but their own first-chart snippets are not\ntests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:30:/** Answers the snippet's CDN URLs from the packed files, by their path in the tarball, as the CDN would. */\ntests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:51:/** Every input of ours that esbuild bundled came from the fixture, never from packages/. */\ntests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:53:  expect(inputs.filter(p => p.includes(`${path.sep}packages${path.sep}`) && !inside(fixture(name), p))).toEqual([]);\ntests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:88:  it('importing the package changes nothing in the document until a chart is created', async () => {\ntests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts:110:describe('script tag: examples/first-chart/script.html, with the CDN URLs answered from the packed files', () => {\ntests/dist/csp.browser.test.ts:2: * Spec DX8, the browser half: the packed files under a strict Content Security Policy sent as a real\ntests/dist/csp.browser.test.ts:49: * The light-scheme default for the first series, as the packed stylesheet declares it. Read whatever form the\ntests/dist/setup.ts:1:// Packs packages/*/dist once per run and installs the tarballs into the fixtures (scripts/pack.mjs). Set\ntests/dist/setup.ts:2:// AXYLO_DIST_BUILD=1 to run the root build first; by default the dist already on disk is packed.\ntests/dist/setup.ts:3:// @ts-expect-error scripts/pack.mjs is plain JavaScript without declarations\ntests/dist/setup.ts:4:import { pack } from '../../scripts/pack.mjs';\ntests/dist/setup.ts:7:  (pack as (options: { build: boolean; log: (line: string) => void }) => unknown)({\ntests/dist/setup.ts:9:    log: line => console.log(`[pack] ${line}`),\ntests/dist/snippets.test.ts:5: * not print one; first-chart.browser.test.ts shows it is not required. The fixtures and the package README\ntests/dist/snippets.test.ts:14:  { file: 'npm.ts', fixture: 'npm', readme: 'packages/axylo/README.md' },\ntests/dist/snippets.test.ts:15:  { file: 'script.html', fixture: 'script', readme: 'packages/axylo/README.md' },\ntests/dist/snippets.test.ts:51:  it('is copied verbatim into its fixture and its package README', () => {\ntests/dist/pages/charts.ts:5: * script (window.Axylo from the script-tag file) and into a module that imports the package from a fixture.\ntests/dist/fixtures/script/package.json:4:  \"description\": \"A page that loads the script-tag files. The test serves node_modules/axylo/dist as a CDN would serve the published package; scripts/pack.mjs runs `npm install --offline` here.\",\ntests/dist/fixtures/script/package.json:6:    \"axylo\": \"file:../../.packed/axylo-0.0.0.tgz\"\ntests/dist/.packed/axylo-0.0.0.tgz\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '149,188p' docs/02-product-spec.md && sed -n '38,90p' docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md && cat research/harness/src/libs/noop.js && node -v && npm -v\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '149,188p' docs/02-product-spec.md && sed -n '38,90p' docs/03-plan-typescript-release.md && cat research/harness/src/libs/noop.js && node -v && npm -v\"","aggregated_output":"### 3.5 Diagnostic registry\n\nLevel decides delivery. **Error**: the chart or a series cannot be drawn; the chart shows its error state. **Warning**: something is not as the author gave it; where that means values were left out or changed (F12), the reader sees the note, and the registry's rows say which codes those are (a warning about an option, a name, a colour or a tick label shows none). **Hint**: advice for the author. Errors and warnings print once per code per page in every build; hints print in development builds only. `strict: true` throws on errors and warnings found while validating a create, `update` or `append` call, synchronously from that call. A diagnostic that can only arise later (a contrast check after the page's CSS changes, a custom formatter that throws when a table page is built, a label that stops fitting after a resize) is reported when it is found and is never thrown. Every diagnostic names the chart; those about data name the field and the first row indexes in the caller's own data.\n\n| Code | Level | Condition | What is drawn |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AX100 | Error | Typed columns have different lengths | Error state; the message names the columns and their lengths |\n| AX101 | Error | A named field is not a key of any row | Error state; the message lists the keys that exist and the closest match |\n| AX102 | Warning | A field is absent (`undefined`) in some rows | Gaps |\n| AX103 | Warning | A value is `NaN` or infinite | Gap |\n| AX104 | Hint | Every non-missing value of a value field is a plain decimal string (`'40'`, `'-1.5'`) | Parsed and drawn; the message suggests `parse: 'number'`. An empty string counts as missing |\n| AX105 | Hint | Steps are absent on a regular time, date, wall-clock or number axis | Gaps. When a series would need more absent steps than twice its observations (and more than 1,000), it is treated as irregular instead: no gaps are created and the hint says so |\n| AX106 | Warning | A value field mixes numbers with strings, or holds strings that are not plain decimals (`'1,234'`, `'n/a'`) | The strings are not drawn |\n| AX107 | Warning | A date or time cannot be parsed | That row is not drawn |\n| AX108 | Error | Duplicate x within a series, or duplicate donut labels | That series, or the donut, is not drawn |\n| AX109 | Hint | Numbers on an axis declared `time` look like seconds, or a numeric x looks like epoch milliseconds without `type: 'time'` | As declared |\n| AX110 | Warning | An author domain on bar or area excluded zero | Domain widened to zero |\n| AX111 | Hint | Instants look like calendar dates | As instants, zone shown |\n| AX112 | Hint | Date-time strings have no offset | As written |\n| AX120 | Error | Negative donut value | Error state |\n| AX121 | Warning | More than eight donut slices | Seven largest plus \"Other (n)\" |\n| AX130 | Warning | More than eight series | All series, with dash or marker differences |\n| AX140 | Warning | No `title` and no `labelledBy` | Generated name |\n| AX141 | Warning | Palette below 3:1 on the resolved background | As themed |\n| AX142 | Hint | Plot too small to draw | Summary and table control |\n| AX143 | Hint | Labels hidden after every remedy | Note shown to the reader |\n| AX150 | Warning | Unknown option key | Ignored; the message suggests the closest known key |\n| AX151 | Warning | `append` rows out of order | Accepted through the slower full update |\n| AX131 | Hint | A compact chart has more than one series | Drawn, with dash differences |\n| AX132 | Hint | More bars than pixels along the category axis | Drawn; the message suggests aggregating |\n| AX133 | Hint | A scatter chart has more than 50,000 points | Drawn; the message says drawing may be slow |\n| AX134 | Error | Series × x positions exceeds 20,000,000 (long rows with many series and little shared x) | Error state; the message gives both counts and suggests fewer series or a scatter chart |\n| AX152 | Warning | `timeZone` is not a zone the browser knows | The viewer's zone is used |\n| AX160 | Warning | A custom formatter threw | The default format is used for that value. A value formatter that throws changes how a value reads, so the reader's note (F12) is shown; a tick formatter that throws only changes an axis label, which is not a value left out or changed, so it is reported without a note (and so the note can never change which ticks fit) |\n| AX199 | Error | An error was thrown while Axylo was building the chart: by Axylo itself, or by code the author supplied that Axylo was running (a row getter, a callback; a formatter that throws is AX160, and the default format is used) | Error state with a generic message; the error is passed to `onDiagnostic` and printed |\n\nExpected results for the Phase 1 fixtures: the combined `dirty` fixture (`[10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70]`) yields AX102, AX103 and AX106 once each, draws Mon–Tue as a segment and Sun as a point, and shows the F12 note. `dirty-string` (one `'40'` among numbers) yields AX106. A column made only of numeric strings yields AX104 and is drawn in full. `dirty-null` yields nothing.\n\nThe split between AX104 and AX106 answers a reviewer's objection that common back ends return counts as strings (Postgres `bigint` and `numeric`, BigQuery): a whole column of plain decimal strings is unambiguous and is parsed; a stray string among numbers is a bug and is not.\n\n### 1.2 Data: one logical table, three forms\n\n```ts\n// long rows: one row per (x, series)\nline(el, { data: rows, x: 'day', y: 'sessions', series: 'channel' });\n\n// wide rows: one column per series\nline(el, { data: wide, x: 'day', y: ['direct', 'organic', { field: 'referral', label: 'Referral' }] });\n\n// typed columns for large data; the row type is inferred from the columns\nline(el, { data: { columns: { t: new Float64Array(n), v: new Float32Array(n) } }, x: { field: 't', type: 'time' }, y: 'v' });\n```\n\nLong and wide are mutually exclusive in the types: `series` cannot be combined with an array of `y`.\n\nRules the three forms share:\n\n| Rule | Detail |\n|---|---|\n| Ownership | Row arrays are read once and never mutated. Typed columns are borrowed, not copied; the caller must not change them in place, and replaces them through `update`. |\n| Column lengths | All columns must have the same length; otherwise AX100. |\n| Missing values | Rows: `null`, or an absent key. Typed columns: `NaN` means missing and does not raise AX103. |\n| Order | Line, area and scatter are sorted by x internally (F11). `append` expects rows at or after the last x. |\n| Provenance | Every normalized sample keeps the index of the row it came from, so diagnostics, the table and events point at the caller's own data. |\n\n### 1.3 Fields\n\nA field is a key of the row, or an object when it needs more. The key is checked against the row type by role: a value axis accepts number fields; text fields are accepted there only with `parse: 'number'`.\n\n```ts\nline(el, {\n  data: samples,\n  x: { field: 'ts', type: 'time', timeZone: 'UTC' },\n  y: { field: 'sessions', label: 'Sessions', unit: 'sessions', tickFormat: { notation: 'compact' } },\n});\n\n// counts that a database driver returns as strings\nbar(el, { data: pgRows, x: 'day', y: { field: 'count', parse: 'number', missing: 'zero' } });\n```\n\n| Option | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `field` | Key of the row. |\n| `label`, `unit` | Axis title; name and unit in tooltip, table and announcements. |\n| `type` (x) | `'date'`, `'time'`, `'number'`, `'category'`. Inferred when omitted, except that a number is never inferred to be an instant (F4). |\n| `timeZone` (x) | For instants: `'local'` (default), `'UTC'`, or an IANA zone. |\n| `format`, `tickFormat` | Readouts and ticks are formatted separately (F6). |\n| `scale` (value) | `'percent'` (0–100) or `'ratio'` (0–1). Declared, never inferred (F7). |\n| `missing` (value) | `'gap'` (default) or `'zero'` (F2). |\n| `parse` (value) | `'number'`, for a text field holding numbers (AX104, AX106). |\n| `domain` | Author bounds. Widened to zero on bar and area (F1). |\n\n### 1.4 Common options\n// Measurement floor: an adapter that draws nothing. Whatever main-thread time the probe reports for this is the harness and the browser, not a chart.\nexport const meta = { name: 'No chart (measurement floor)', pkg: null };\nexport function scale(el) { el.textContent = ''; return { destroy() {} }; }\nexport function stream(el) { return { push() {}, destroy() {} }; }\nv24.21.0\n11.19.0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
