null` and `index: -1`; check before you look a row up.\napps/docs/pages/options.md:5:Types are written in TypeScript. `Row` is the type of one of your rows (for typed columns it is inferred from the columns), `Options` the options type of the chart, and `XValue` is `number | string | Date`, a value on an x axis.\napps/docs/pages/options.md:29:| `data` | `Data<Row>` | required | The rows (`readonly Row[]`), or `{ columns }` with one array or typed array per field, all of equal length. See [Your data](data.md). |\napps/docs/pages/options.md:212:| `row` | `Row \\| null` | Your row; with typed columns, an object built from the columns at that index; `null` for a position no row holds. |\napps/docs/pages/updating.md:87:- `row` is your own row object (with typed columns, an object built from the columns at that index), and `index` its index in your data. A position no row of yours holds (an inferred missing step, a donut's \"Other\") has `row: null` and `index: -1`.\npackages/axylo/src/dom/swatch.ts:16:  /** Palette index of the series (or slice), null for a muted entry such as a donut's \"Other\". */\npackages/axylo/src/dom/swatch.ts:113:  // Bars, areas and donut slices are filled regions: a square chip. Otherwise the series' marker.\npackages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:209:      const segments = compact ? null : model.noteSegments ?? null;\npackages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:210:      if (segments && segments.length > 1) {\npackages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:214:        const signature = segments.map(run => `${run.lang ?? ''}\\u0001${run.text}`).join('\\u0002');\npackages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:216:          note.replaceChildren(...segments.map(run => {\npackages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:229:        setText(note, compact ? '' : segments?.[0]?.text ?? model.note ?? '');\npackages/axylo/src/dom/figure.ts:230:        setAttr(note, 'lang', segments ? segments[0]?.lang ?? null : model.noteLang ?? null);\npackages/axylo/src/index.ts:11:import { DONUT } from './kinds/donut';\npackag